Target first, then read its Base Cost (AlteredBGA, apply with `patch -p1`)

Angry Crowd (YZ / OD Rare: "Discard target Character or Permanent. If its Base Cost was {2} or less,
create a Manaseed token") and Partial Referee (YZ Common / Rare, MU Rare: "Discard target
Character. If its Base Cost was {3} or more, its controller draws a card") were an XOR of two
Target actions, one per cost range: the player first chose "a target of cost 2 or less" or "a
target of cost 3 or more", then the target among those. The cost only decides the bonus, not a
choice the card offers.

Fix: one Target over every legal card; its effect is a CheckCondition on the new condition
`baseCostCheck:COST:OP` (the target's Base Cost: Reserve Cost if Fleeting, else Hand Cost, as
Target's maxBaseCost / minBaseCost), read before the discard: met, discard then the bonus;
otherwise, discard only. The Rust translation has the same condition
(rules/src/helpers/conditions.rs base_cost_check) and the cards' data is exported from this code.

Checked: the per-card goldens of the five cards recorded again with this patch and replayed by the
Rust engine (137 nodes); rules/tests/target_then_cost.rs plays each card on its rich board, checks
that the first decision is the target (cards of both cost ranges in it), then for every target that
the Manaseed is created / the card drawn exactly when the Base Cost condition holds.

